### Colab API — confirmed

Google Colab DOES have an official programmatic API.

The current Colab API is beta and allowlist-based.

Official service:

`https://colaboratory.googleapis.com`

It supports:

- list runtimes
- create managed runtime
- get runtime
- delete runtime
- list runtime specifications
- long-running operation tracking

Runtime creation:

`POST https://colaboratory.googleapis.com/v1beta/runtimes`

It requires the Colab OAuth scope:

`https://www.googleapis.com/auth/colaboratory`

Runtime creation returns a long-running Operation. Runtime objects expose connection information including a URL and short-lived proxy token.

IMPORTANT: Creating a Colab runtime creates a managed Jupyter runtime; it does NOT by itself guarantee that a particular notebook has executed its cells.

Therefore the lifecycle must be:

Colab runtime requested
→ runtime created
→ runtime connection available
→ worker bootstrap executed
→ worker registered
